Here is a **complete, production-ready academic conference submission system** designed as a **single-page web application** with progressive enhancement for mobile. It integrates:

- PDF paper uploads
- Automated format compliance checker (pages, font, margins)
- Double-blind review mode (auto-removal of author info)
- Submission progress tracking
- Plagiarism detection (simulated via Turnitin-style API)
- Responsive UI with dark academia aesthetic

---

## ✅ Features

| Feature                     | Description                                                                 |
|----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **PDF Upload**             | Dropzone + file validation (≤20MB, PDF only)                               |
| **Format Checker**         | OCR-free heuristic: page count, font size, margin ratios                   |
| **Double-Blind Mode**      | Toggle to anonymize authors, titles, affiliations                         |
| **Progress Tracking**      | Visual progress bar + step-by-step wizard                                 |
| **Plagiarism Detection**   | Simulated API call with mock Turnitin-style score + report                 |
| **Responsive**             | Mobile-first design with touch-friendly controls                           |
| **Local Storage**          | Persists progress across sessions                                          |

---

## 📁 Tech Stack

- **Frontend**: Vanilla HTML, CSS (Tailwind CSS), JavaScript (ES6+)
- **PDF Processing**: `pdf-lib` (in-browser via `pdf-lib@latest` via CDN) — *note: limited browser support; use worker fallback*
- **OCR-Free Heuristic**: DOM-based extraction (PDF text extracted via `pdf-lib` → `text-extract` via JS)
- **Turnitin Simulation**: Mock API with weighted scoring
- **Storage**: `localStorage` + IndexedDB fallback

